[ system ]
{# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   A SECOND LOOK BEFORE A BETRAYAL COSTS ANYTHING (2.2, WP-N).

   snrom_talk_assess may answer BETRAYAL, and Papyrus then lands the bond far
   below Stranger in one step: months of play, gone in a call. A model that
   misreads one conversation, or invents a line, would do that to a
   relationship nothing was wrong with. So the largest cost is never paid on
   one reading. This call sees the act the first one quoted, the person, and
   the record, and answers whether it happened and what it was.

   It may agree, scale it down to a serious wrong, or find nothing. It may not
   scale anything UP: the first call already judged the size, and this one
   exists only to stop an error. The answers are words; Papyrus maps them.

   Same three sources, same order, as snrom_talk_assess (dialogue, memories,
   diary, least guarded nearest the question), and the same counter to the
   profile's roleplay heading. No example of a betrayal anywhere in here: in
   this project an illustration is copied back as the answer.
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ #}
You check one judgement before it is acted on. Another reader decided that {{ player.name }} betrayed {{ npc_name }}, and quoted what they did. Acting on that changes everything between them, so it is checked first, against the record and against who {{ npc_name }} is.

Three questions, in order. Stop at the first one that fails.

1. DID IT HAPPEN? The record that follows must show {{ player.name }} doing what the quote is about: said, remembered or written. The quote may be {{ player.name }}'s own words, or someone's account of what {{ player.name }} did - {{ npc_name }} confronting them about it counts as the record showing it. Close wording is enough; an act the record does not show at all is not. It must be {{ player.name }}'s doing: something done between two other people is not {{ player.name }}'s act.

2. DO THEY KNOW? {{ npc_name }} must have seen it, been part of it, or been told. Something they never learned has not touched what they feel, however it would land if they did.

3. WAS IT A BETRAYAL TO THEM? A betrayal breaks what the bond itself rested on, as {{ npc_name }} understood it: a trust they had placed, a promise the whole relationship assumed, a loyalty they had every reason to count on. Judge it by them. What one person would count as the end of everything, another would shrug off or never have expected in the first place; their profile says which kind of person they are. Hurt, anger and a serious wrong are not by themselves a betrayal: those are real, and they are smaller.

An answer that ends a relationship needs the evidence in front of you. If you cannot find the act, or cannot tell whether they know, the answer is the smaller one or nothing - never the largest by default.

[ user ]
{% set npc_uuid = formid_to_uuid(npc_formid) %}
WHO THEY ARE
{% set profile = "" %}
{% if npc_uuid and npc_uuid != 0 %}
{% set profile = render_character_profile("transform", npc_uuid) %}
{% endif %}
{% if profile and profile != "" %}
{{ profile }}
{% else %}
{{ npc_name }} - no profile available.
{% endif %}

WHAT WAS SAID - between {{ npc_name }} and {{ player.name }}, most recent last
{% if npc_uuid and npc_uuid != 0 %}
{% set _filter = [] %}
{% set _filter = append(_filter, npc_uuid) %}
{% set events = get_recent_events(300, _filter) %}
{% else %}
{% set events = get_recent_events(40) %}
{% endif %}
{% set said = [] %}
{% for ev in events %}
{% if existsIn(ev.data, "dialogue") %}
{% if ev.type == "dialogue" and existsIn(ev.data, "speaker") and existsIn(ev.data, "listener") %}
{% if (ev.data.speaker == npc_name and ev.data.listener == player.name) or (ev.data.speaker == player.name and ev.data.listener == npc_name) %}
{% set said = append(said, ev) %}
{% endif %}
{% elif ev.type == "dialogue_player_text" or ev.type == "dialogue_player_stt" %}
{% if not existsIn(ev.data, "listener") or ev.data.listener == npc_name %}
{% set said = append(said, ev) %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if exists("npc_since_sec") and npc_since_sec > 0 %}
{% set fresh = [] %}
{% for ev in said %}{% if ev.gameTime >= npc_since_sec %}{% set fresh = append(fresh, ev) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% set said = fresh %}
{% endif %}
{% if length(said) > 0 %}
{% for ev in said %}
[{{ ev.gameTimeStr }}] {{ default(ev.data.speaker, player.name) }}: {{ ev.data.dialogue }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
Nothing has passed between them recently.
{% endif %}

{% set mem = get_relevant_memories(npc_uuid, 4) %}
{% if mem and length(mem) > 0 %}
WHAT THEY KEPT - things they have held onto
{% for m in mem %}
- {{ m.memory.content }}{% if m.memory.emotion %} ({{ m.memory.emotion }}){% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% set diaries = get_diary_entries(npc_uuid, 3) %}
{% if diaries and length(diaries) > 0 %}
THEIR OWN ACCOUNT, IN PRIVATE
{% for e in diaries %}
[{{ e.entry_date_str }}] {{ e.content }}{% if e.emotion %} ({{ e.emotion }}){% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

THE JUDGEMENT BEING CHECKED
The act, as quoted: {{ harm_act }}
How it was read: {{ harm_what }}

**You are not {{ npc_name }}. You are checking a judgement about them.** The profile above is headed as though you were about to play them; that heading belongs to a different task. Do not answer in character. Its "What You Know About" section is generated from a counter of interactions and is often wrong about how well they know each other; where it disagrees with the record, disregard it.

Answer in exactly this form and nothing else:

NAME: {{ npc_name }}
VERDICT: <BETRAYAL|WOUND|NONE>   <- `BETRAYAL` only if all three questions hold. `WOUND` if it happened and they know, and it was a serious wrong but not a betrayal to them. `NONE` if it is not in the record, was not {{ player.name }}'s act against them, or they do not know.
WHY: <one sentence: which question decided it, and what in the record shows it>
